  protoOf(WhatsNew).g5l = function () {
    return this.w1n("<!--\nIn-app What's New. Shown once, on the first launch after an update.\n\nNewest version first. Each section is a heading `##` plus the version, then 3 to 5 items.\nAn item is an SF Symbol the design system already uses, a bold title of at most four words, and one plain line of at most 90 characters.\nUser-facing words only. No build numbers and no lane codes.\nEvery release adds a section at the top, in the same commit as the store release notes.\n\nTestFlight builds (Roberto, 25 Oct 2026: \"Show it after every build\"). Each TestFlight build gets its own section,\n`## 1.3.10 (143)`: the version, a space and the build number in brackets. Same item format (icon, title of at most\nfour words, one line of at most 90 characters), 1 to 5 items, newest build first, above the version section.\nReleases adds it in the same commit as that build's What to Test. A TestFlight install shows its build's section once,\nmerged with the sections of builds it skipped (at most 5 items, newest first); a build without its own section shows\nnothing. The App Store install shows only the version section (`## 1.3.10`), once per version; keep that section.\n-->\n\n## 1.3.11 (158)\n\n- icon: figure.run\n  **Body**\n  A wellness day shows the body strip and reader.\n\n- icon: thermometer.medium\n  **Sauna and Yoga**\n  Every tap counts. Yoga repeats while held. iPad shows the card first.\n\n- icon: heart.fill\n  **Heart rate**\n  A dropped link returns, and a reading stays fresh for 10 s.\n\n- icon: timer\n  **Timers agree**\n  The Dynamic Island keeps ticking and matches the workout.\n\n- icon: checkmark.circle.fill\n  **Not recorded**\n  A run with no distance reads Not recorded.\n\n## 1.3.10 (153)\n\n- icon: chart.xyaxis.line\n  **Cardiac drift**\n  A straight trend line, with a dot for each rep.\n\n- icon: list.bullet\n  **Distance reps count**\n  Drift counts each rep on a distance plan.\n\n- icon: checkmark.circle.fill\n  **Summary stays put**\n  View post no longer brings the finish summary back.\n\n## 1.3.10 (152)\n\n- icon: pencil\n  **Edit from a post**\n  Opens that activity, including sauna, yoga, and ones not on this device yet.\n\n- icon: checkmark.circle.fill\n  **Summary right away**\n  The summary appears as soon as you finish.\n\n- icon: list.bullet\n  **Titles on one line**\n  Avg pace, Avg speed and Drift stay on a single line.\n\n- icon: ellipsis\n  **Live bar stays open**\n  The top bar no longer folds into an empty menu pill.\n\n- icon: app.connected.to.app.below.fill\n  **Connected apps stays open**\n  Intervals.icu detail no longer freezes the page while it loads.\n\n## 1.3.10 (151)\n\n- icon: person.2\n  **Community share switch**\n  Turning Community off unposts that activity.\n\n- icon: square.and.arrow.up\n  **Strava locks once posted**\n  Strava locks once posted, and Remove is on Strava.\n\n- icon: thermometer.medium\n  **Sauna temperature**\n  Minus and plus change it during the session, and the average is prefilled.\n\n- icon: heart.fill\n  **Sauna and yoga heart**\n  A finished sauna or yoga shows its heart-rate chart.\n\n- icon: bicycle\n  **Trainer steps once**\n  Each tap of plus or minus steps the trainer once.\n\n## 1.3.10 (150)\n\n- icon: square.and.arrow.up\n  **Share to Strava**\n  Share to Strava is on every finished activity.\n\n- icon: chart.xyaxis.line\n  **Cleaner finished charts**\n  Finished charts leave out a 0 W start and speed spikes.\n\n- icon: bicycle\n  **Ride drift and zones**\n  A ride shows its drift and heart-rate zones.\n\n- icon: flame.fill\n  **Calorie split**\n  The calorie split follows published data.\n\n- icon: pencil\n  **Back to that day**\n  Closing an activity takes you back to that day.\n\n## 1.3.10 (149)\n\n- icon: checkmark.circle.fill\n  **Finish on first tap**\n  Finish works on the first tap.\n\n- icon: arrow.up\n  **Ascent on outdoor runs**\n  Outdoor runs show the ascent you climbed.\n\n## 1.3.10 (148)\n\n- icon: checkmark.circle.fill\n  **Ask Coach works again**\n  Your question is sent even while your history refreshes.\n\n- icon: pencil\n  **Coach says if blocked**\n  If Coach can't read your training, it says so and nothing is sent.\n\n## 1.3.10 (147)\n\n- icon: flag.checkered\n  **Predictor uses one run**\n  Your best recent run sets 5K to 100K, and one line names that run.\n\n- icon: list.bullet\n  **Runs right after launch**\n  Race Predictor shows your runs right after you open it.\n\n- icon: square.and.arrow.up\n  **Share sheet stays up**\n  If one card fails, the rest of the share sheet still works.\n\n- icon: pencil\n  **Feedback includes shares**\n  A share that fails is included when you send feedback.\n\n## 1.3.10 (146)\n\n- icon: square.and.arrow.up\n  **New sticker cards**\n  Share Stats, Route, Splits, Day or a big number as a transparent sticker, or a Map card.\n\n- icon: flag.checkered\n  **Predictor counts long runs**\n  Long runs and 15, 20 and 30 km stretches now count, and it updates after every run.\n\n- icon: ruler\n  **Cards follow your units**\n  The share cards follow the km/miles setting straight away.\n\n## 1.3.10 (145)\n\n- icon: square.and.arrow.up\n  **One Share per story**\n  An open story keeps its own Share. The top Share, which posted to followers, is gone.\n\n- icon: checkmark.circle.fill\n  **Share sheet on iPad**\n  On iPad, the \"Change a tile\" tip no longer appears over the share sheet.\n\n## 1.3.10 (144)\n\n- icon: checkmark.circle.fill\n  **Every TestFlight update**\n  What's New appears again after each TestFlight update.\n\n## 1.3.10\n\n- icon: flag.checkered\n  **Next step**\n  A step tile counts down to the next target and shows a finish flag on the last step.\n\n- icon: bicycle\n  **Ride replay**\n  A ride replay lasts at least the moving time. Kilometer markers never overlap.\n\n- icon: checkmark.circle.fill\n  **Finished activity**\n  A finished activity opens instantly from the data saved with it. Share comes after Replay.\n\n- icon: pencil\n  **Imported activities**\n  Imported activities no longer ask for a name.\n\n- icon: list.bullet\n  **Spoken tiles**\n  Each tile is spoken as one item on iPhone and Android.\n");
  };
